Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.43,0:00:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,How do engineers build these systems There are several\Napproaches In one superconducting
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.24,0:00:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,circuits operate at extremely low temperatures inside\Nspecialized equipment In another
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.49,0:00:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,trapped ions are controlled using electromagnetic fields\Nand lasers Other platforms are
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.37,0:00:20.73,Default,,0,0,0,,also being researched We should not imagine that every\Nquantum computer is built in the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.74,0:00:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,same way The glowing forest represents a world of ideas\Nin the laboratory there are
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.59,0:00:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,instruments calibration electronic control and extensive\Nengineering Classical computers
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.04,0:00:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,continue to participate they organize tasks control\Nequipment and analyze results In
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.43,0:00:40.47,Default,,0,0,0,,practice these technologies work together rather than as\Nrivals that need to replace each
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.48,0:00:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,other